      "role": "Leader",
      "highlight": true,
      "printGroup": "led",
      "place": "Università degli Studi di Sassari, Alghero, Italy",
      "details": "The workshop invited participants to reflect on how the design of many products is shaped by the biases and perspectives of both designers and users — aspects that manifest in visual language. Certain design choices send signals that lead some users to feel recognised and welcomed, while others contribute to dynamics of discrimination or marginalisation. The goal was to learn to identify these mechanisms through analysis and design experimentation, developing concrete proposals that rethought the visual language of products in a more conscious, sensitive, and responsible way.\n\n**Participants:** 1st–3rd year BSc Design students.\n**Role:** Workshop leader — prepared agenda, activities, and facilitated development.",
